H7928H.def:
A man of the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 7:19; 
son of: Shemida (H8061); 
brother of: Ahian (H0291), Likhi (H3949) and Aniam (H0593)
§ Shechem = "back" or "shoulder"
1) son of Gilead and grandson of Manasseh
2) a Manassite, son of Shemida

H7930.def:
Someone descended from Shechem who was a man of the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Nombres 26:31; 
son of: Gilead (H1568H); 
brother of: Abiezer (H0044I), Helek (H2507), Asriel (H0844), Shemida (H8061) and Hepher (H2660A)
Group of she.khem (שֶׁ֫כֶם "Shechem" H7928) 
§ Shechemites = "shoulder"
descendants of Shechem

H7940G.def:
A man of the tribe of Levi living at the time of United Monarchy, only mentioned at 1 Chroniques 26:4; 
son of: Obed-edom (H5654); 
brother of: Shemaiah (H8098I), Jehozabad (H3075H), Joah (H3098I), Nethanel (H5417K), Ammiel (H5988I), Issachar (H3485H) and Peullethai (H6469)
§ Sacar = "wages"
1) father of Ahiam, one of David's mighty warriors
2) a Korahite Levite gatekeeper, the 4th son of Obed-edom in the time of David

H7940H.def:
A man living at the time of United Monarchy, first mentioned at 2 Samuel 23:33; 
father of: Ahiam (H0279); also called Sachar (KJV: Sacar; NIV: Sakar) at 1 Chroniques 11:35;
Another name of sha.rar (שָׁרָר "Sharar" H8325)
§ Sacar = "wages"
1) father of Ahiam, one of David's mighty warriors
2) a Korahite Levite gatekeeper, the 4th son of Obed-edom in the time of David

H7956.def:
A man of the tribe of Judah living at the time of Egypt and Wilderness, first mentioned at Genèse 38:5; 
son of: Judah (H3063) and Bath-shua (H1323I); 
brother of: Er (H6147) and Onan (H0209); 
half-brother of: Perez (H6557) and Zerah (H2226I); 
father of: Er (H6147H), Laadah (H3935), Jokim (H3137), Joash (H3101K) and Saraph (H8315); also called Shelanite at Nombres 26:20; 
Also named: she.la.ni (שֵׁלָנִי "Shelanite" H8024) 
§ Shelah = "a petition"
the youngest son of Judah

H7974.def:
A man living at the time of the Patriarchs, first mentioned at Genèse 10:24; 
son of: Cainan (G2536); 
father of: Eber (H5677)
Also named: Sala (Σαλά "Shelah" G4527H) 
§ Salah or Shelah = "sprout"
son of Arphaxad and father of Eber
